      "artist": "InSapphoWeTrust from Los Angeles, California, USA",
      "description": "Calico, a ghost town located in Yermo halfway between Los Angeles and Las Vegas, was once a very productive silver mining town, home to over 3,000 people in the 1880s. The decline in silver prices killed the mines in 1896, and the town shriveled to nothing. Today's Calico is a 1950s reconstruction by Walter Knott (of Knott's Berry Farm in Buena Park) on top of the original building foundations, donated to the County of San Bernardino in 1967.\n\nI am on the Calico &amp; Odessa Railroad, as the train wraps up its final run of the day, and as the sun sets. Here is a look at the parking lot, the campground, and some desert homes outside town on the way to Yermo and I-15.",
